# Environment variable contract
#
# This file is a TEMPLATE. Every value is intentionally empty. Never commit a
# real key, token, password, or connection string — copy this file to `.env`
# (git-ignored) and fill it in locally.
#
# Vite splits environment variables into two buckets, and the boundary is a
# security boundary:
#
#   1. `VITE_*`      -> injected into the browser bundle at BUILD time. Anything
#                       you can read in DevTools or in the shipped `dist/` JS.
#                       Treat these as PUBLIC. Never put a secret here.
#   2. everything else -> not reachable by the browser at all. A Node server
#                       process must read these directly from `process.env`.
#
# This project has no backend yet (that arrives in Phase 3). Until then there are
# no server variables to set, and no AI provider is configured.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Browser-visible (VITE_*) — public by definition, no secrets allowed
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Base URL of the backend API, e.g. http://localhost:3000
# Introduced with the Phase 3 dev proxy. Leave empty to stay in local-chatbot mode.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server-only (NO `VITE_` prefix) — never shipped to the browser
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Listed here so the names are settled before the backend exists. Each stays
# empty until the corresponding phase actually introduces it, and each must be
# read from `process.env` inside `server/`, never imported by `src/`.

# Phase 4 — AI provider credentials. Selected vendor is still an open decision.
# AI_PROVIDER_API_KEY=
# AI_PROVIDER_MODEL=

# Phase 3/8 — API server binding
# PORT=
# NODE_ENV=

# Phase 5 — PostgreSQL. Credentials belong here, never in VITE_* variables.
# DATABASE_URL=